    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Description :</b> The system allows users to create a new product with negative values in the Buying Price and Selling Price fields. Even when negative prices are entered, the product is successfully created and added to the inventory without displaying any validation message. The system should prevent negative price values and display appropriate validation messages to ensure data accuracy and integrity.</p>

<p><b>Precondition :</b> </p>

<ul>
	<li>User is logged in.</li>
	<li>User has permission to create a new product.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Steps to Reproduce:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Navigate to the Product Add page.</li>
	<li>Enter a valid product name.</li>
	<li>Enter a negative value in the Buying Price field (e.g., -100).</li>
	<li>Enter a negative value in the Selling Price field (e.g., -150).</li>
	<li>Fill in all other mandatory fields with valid information.</li>
	<li>Click the Create/Save button.</li>
	<li>Check whether the product is successfully created in the inventory.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Test Data :</b> </p>

<ol>
	<li>Product Name  : Polo T-shirt<br/>
Buying Price     :  -100 ,<br/>
Selling Price     :  -150</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Result :</b> The system should not allow users to enter or save negative values in the Buying Price and Selling Price fields. It should display appropriate validation messages and prevent product creation until valid non-negative prices are provided.</p>

<p><b>Actual Result :</b> The system accepts negative values in both Buying Price and Selling Price fields and successfully creates the product in the inventory.</p>

